<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.12.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00593</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.12.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9f97a300-0971-4a96-99bd-17b002b17ba3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">For 1 - 4, use the following passage:</para>
      <para id="para-00003">
        <quote id="quote-00001">Harrison works two part time jobs. One at a gas station that pays $11 an hour and the
        other is IT troubleshooting for $16.50 an hour. Between the two jobs, Harrison wants to earn
        at least $330 a week. How many hours does Harrison need to work at each job to earn at least
        $330?</quote>
     </para>

        <exercise id="_26e22785-9da2-41bd-817f-c237694558f1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Let x be the number of hours he works at the gas station and let y be the
              number of hours he works troubleshooting. Which inequality correctly models this
              situation?</para>
            <para id="para-00005">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00006">\(11x + 16.5y ≥ 330\)</para>
            <para id="para-00007">\(16.5x + 11y ≥ 330\)</para>
            <para id="para-00008">\(11x + 16.5y ≤ 330\)</para>
            <para id="para-00009">\(16.5y + 11x > 330\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00010">Correct! He makes 11x dollars at the gas station and \(16.5y\) dollars
              troubleshooting. The sum must be greater than or equal to 330 dollars.</para>
            <para id="para-00011">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00012">The correct answer is \(11x + 16.5y ≥ 330\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_72ff8696-a5af-4446-98e7-adb762dc606a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00013">Which graph correctly represents the inequality from the previous question?</para>
            <para id="para-00014">a.</para>
            <para id="para-00015">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 10 and the \(x\)-axis at 15. The region above the line is shaded.

">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_01.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00016">b.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 30 and the \(x\)-axis at 20. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00018">c.</para>
            <para id="para-00019">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 20 and the \(x\)-axis at 30. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_03.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00020">d.</para>
            <para id="para-00021">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 30 and the \(x\)-axis at 20. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_04.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00022">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00023">a</para>
            <para id="para-00024">b</para>
            <para id="para-00025">c</para>
            <para id="para-00026">d</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00027">Correct! 
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 20 and the \(x\)-axis at 30. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_05.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00028">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00029">The correct answer is c.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d28ed77f-752b-4446-b08e-44cc2b64267f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00030">Which of the following ordered pairs is a solution to the inequality?</para>
            <para id="para-00031">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00032">(10, 20)</para>
            <para id="para-00033">(25, 2)</para>
            <para id="para-00034">(15, 9)</para>
            <para id="para-00035">(3, 17)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00036">Correct! \(11(10) + 16.5(20) = 440\), which is greater than 330</para>
            <para id="para-00037">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00038">The correct answer is \((10, 20)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="b1d49162-ffed-4194-8ad1-c28d4588ff57" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00039">Which of the following is true about the solution you found in the previous
              question?</para>
            <para id="para-00040">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00041">The <emphasis effect="italics">y</emphasis>-coordinate represents how many hours
              Harrison will work at the gas station.</para>
            <para id="para-00042">The <emphasis effect="italics">x</emphasis>-coordinate represents how many hours
              he works at the IT job.</para>
            <para id="para-00043">The solution represents a work schedule that earns him more than $330 per week.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00044">Correct! The solution represents a work schedule where he earns 11x dollars at the
              gas station and \(16.5y \) dollars troubleshooting to earn more than $330 per week.</para>
            <para id="para-00045">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00046">The correct answer is that the solution represents a work schedule that earns him
              more than $330 per week..</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <para id="para-00047">For 5 - 8, use the following passage:</para>
      <para id="para-00048">
        <quote id="quote-00002">The doctor tells Maya she needs to exercise enough to burn 500 calories each day. She
        likes to run which burns 15 calories per minute or bike which burns 10 calories per minute.</quote>
     </para>

        <exercise id="_97fccdef-959e-4130-8142-8133b6bd32aa" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00049">If x is the number of minutes that Maya runs and y is the number of minutes she
              bikes, find the inequality that models the situation.</para>
            <para id="para-00050">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00051">\(15x + 10y &lt; 500\)</para>
            <para id="para-00052">\(15x + 10y ≥ 500\)</para>
            <para id="para-00053">\(15x + 10y > 500\)</para>
            <para id="para-00054">15x + 10y ≤ 500</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00055">Correct! She burns 15x calories running and \(10y\) calories biking. The total
              calories must be greater than or equal to 500.</para>
            <para id="para-00056">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00057">The correct answer is \(15x + 10y ≥ 500\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8e39b40d-f7f7-49fe-b845-0e77b6694c70" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00058">Which graph correctly represents the inequality from the previous question?</para>
            <para id="para-00059">a.</para>
            <para id="para-00060">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 25 and the \(x\)-axis at 35. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_06.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00061">b.</para>
            <para id="para-00062">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 50 and the \(x\)-axis at 20. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_07.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00063">c.</para>
            <para id="para-00064">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 50 and the \(x\)-axis at about 33. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_08.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00065">d.</para>
            <para id="para-00066">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at about 33 and the \(x\)-axis at 50. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_09.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00067">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00068">a</para>
            <para id="para-00069">b</para>
            <para id="para-00070">c</para>
            <para id="para-00071">d</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00072">Correct! 
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 50 and the \(x\)-axis at about 33. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_10.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00073">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00074">The correct answer is c.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_31d8c372-5855-4b11-ae98-f692906a6709" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00075">Which of the following ordered pairs is a solution to the inequality?</para>
            <para id="para-00076">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00077">(5, 40)</para>
            <para id="para-00078">(15, 30)</para>
            <para id="para-00079">(20, 15)</para>
            <para id="para-00080">(25, 10)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00081">Correct! \(15(15) + 10(30) = 525\), which is greater than 500.</para>
            <para id="para-00082">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00083">The correct answer is \((15, 30)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a1edcba0-490d-476a-b91f-6377952ab355" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00084">Which of the following is true about the solution you found in the previous
              question?</para>
            <para id="para-00085">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00086">The <emphasis effect="italics">x</emphasis>-coordinate represents the number of
              minutes that Maya bikes.</para>
            <para id="para-00087">The <emphasis effect="italics">y</emphasis>-coordinate represents the number of
              minutes that Maya runs.</para>
            <para id="para-00088">The solution represents a workout which allows Maya to burn at least 500 calories.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00089">Correct! The solution represents a workout where she burns \(15x\) calories
              running and 10y calories biking to burn more than 500 calories.</para>
            <para id="para-00090">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00091">The correct answer is that the solution represents a workout which allows Maya to
              burn at least 500 calories.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <para id="para-00092"> For 9 - 12, use the following passage:</para>
      <para id="para-00093">
        <quote id="quote-00003">Armando’s workouts consist of kickboxing and swimming. While kickboxing, he burns 10
        calories per minute and he burns 7 calories a minute while swimming. He wants to burn at
        least 600 calories each day.</quote>
     </para>
 
        <exercise id="e80766bc-fccb-4cea-a56e-c149b0767885" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00094">If x is the number of minutes that Armando will kickbox and y is the number of
              minutes he will swim, find the inequality that will help Armando create a workout for
              today.</para>
            <para id="para-00095">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00096">\(7x + 10y ≥ 600\)</para>
            <para id="para-00097">\(7x + 10y &lt; 600\)</para>
            <para id="para-00098">\(10x + 7y > 600\)</para>
            <para id="para-00099">\(10x + 7y ≥ 600\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00100">Correct! He burns 10x calories kickboxing and \(7y\) calories biking. The total
              calories must be greater than or equal to 600.</para>
            <para id="para-00101">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00102">The correct answer is \(10x + 7y ≥ 600\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_3e474b72-0161-45ff-b7af-6c6312952b34" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00103">Which graph correctly represents the inequality from the previous question?</para>
            <para id="para-00104">a.</para>
            <para id="para-00105">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 60 and the \(x\)-axis at about 85. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_11.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00106">b.</para>
            <para id="para-00107">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at about 85 and the \(x\)-axis at 60. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_12.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00108">c.</para>
            <para id="para-00109">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at about 85 and the \(x\)-axis at 30. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_13.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00110">d.</para>
            <para id="para-00111">
              
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 30 and the \(x\)-axis at about 85. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_14.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00112">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00113">a</para>
            <para id="para-00114">b</para>
            <para id="para-00115">c</para>
            <para id="para-00116">d</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00117">Correct !
                <media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 60 and the \(x\)-axis at about 85. The region above the line is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_11_15.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00118">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00119">The correct answer is b.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="eaf21394-aee3-4ead-9f12-cf241d847127" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00011">
            <para id="para-00120">Which of the following ordered pairs is a solution to the inequality?</para>
            <para id="para-00121">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00122">(20, 70)</para>
            <para id="para-00123">(10, 70)</para>
            <para id="para-00124">(30, 40)</para>
            <para id="para-00125">(40, 20)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00011">
            <para id="para-00126">Correct! \(10(20) + 7(70) = 690\), which is greater than 600.</para>
            <para id="para-00127">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00128">The correct answer is \((20, 70)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_25cf4659-a80c-4015-9524-946b2898a7f2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00012">
            <para id="para-00129">Which of the following is true about the solution you found in the previous
              question?</para>
            <para id="para-00130">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00131">The <emphasis effect="italics">x</emphasis>-coordinate represents the number of
              minutes that Armando swims.</para>
            <para id="para-00132">The <emphasis effect="italics">y</emphasis>-coordinate represents the number of
              minutes that Armando swims.</para>
            <para id="para-00133">The solution represents a workout which allows Armando to burn at least 500
              calories.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00012">
            <para id="para-00134">Correct! The problem states that y represents the number of minutes Armando swims.</para>
            <para id="para-00135">Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00136">The correct answer is that the <emphasis effect="italics">y</emphasis>-coordinate
              represents the number of minutes that Armando swims.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    </section>
